  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 129 AM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will remain near the Four Corners region through \nMonday. This will lead to a fairly stagnant forecast. High \ntemperatures will stay hot and near normal each day Saturday through \nWednesday. Humidity will remain low enough to keep heat indices \nbelow Heat Advisory criteria, however a few spots in the Coastal \nPlains could briefly reach criteria each afternoon. With upper ridge \nfarther north a few showers or thunderstorms could move over the \nCoastal Plains each afternoon Sunday and Monday, but chances will be \nmostly less than 20%. As the ridge shifts back toward the southeast, \nrain chances will come to an end.",
